bcoc:StrategicPlanning rdf:type skos:Concept .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning skos:changeNote "2026-10-24, review R6 section 3.4: generalized. The definition named a mission statement, a long-term strategic vision, and enterprise-wide and business-unit strategies. An organization with no business units or no written mission can still plan strategically, so the list made customary practices necessary conditions. It now says what the capability is for. \"Realized in\" became \"realizable in\" (CD8). Every source is now marked contextual (R6 section 6.1)."@en .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning skos:changeNote "2026-10-25, review R7 section 4: \"long-range\" dropped. Planning over a short horizon, or revising aims in response to an event, can be strategic, and the qualifier excluded it. The genus field now names the immediate genus, bco:BusinessCapability: the class the definition's text names and bcom:BusinessCapability designates. cco:ont00000568 (Organization Capability) moved to foundational_ancestor (review R7 Finding E; docs/decisions/2026-10-25-r7-genus-decision.md). Nothing is minted."@en .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning skos:definition "A business capability, inhering in an organization, that is realizable in planned acts by which that organization sets or revises its aims and the courses of action it means to take toward them."@en .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning skos:inScheme bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme .
bcoc:StrategicPlanning skos:prefLabel "Strategic Planning"@en .

