bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:catalogCandidate "BCC-0ba10d44" .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:currentRecord bcoc:record-848bcd712735b60d46cf54564456c9c8ee00dde855881c3497fd3ad6d6a74d88 .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:definitionGenus bco:BusinessCapability .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:foundationalAncestor cco:ont00000568 .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:lifecycleStatus "Draft" .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-3c7c642f5a0179876a5d092352483f454291c7d88136fc6870216096fdac53bc .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-7fbc3e395fbf7b5de65a40d2ae8efb38bd86a1bbd43695fb0d7bf146cb9ae03a .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-aa18f2be9785bc5958d0fc79b9b3d3c15742ece3e290f43d0435a829edd67a81 .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement dcterms:created "2026-10-24T12:14:15+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement prov:wasAttributedTo bcoa:claude-opus-5-5 .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement rdf:type skos:Concept .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:altLabel "Treasury Operations Management"@en .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:broader bcoc:FinancialResourceManagement .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:changeNote "2026-10-24, review R6 section 3.5: generalized. The definition required treasury oversight, cash tracking and reconciliation, an investment policy and a hedging strategy, all four. A small business that manages its liquidity without hedging would have been excluded. It now says what the capability is for: having the means to pay when payment falls due. \"Realized in\" became \"realizable in\" (CD8). Every source is now marked contextual (R6 section 6.1)."@en .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:changeNote "2026-10-25, review R7 section 4: \"ensures\" removed. It made a successful outcome, always having the cash to pay, a condition of having the capability, so an organization that manages its liquidity and still meets a funding shortfall would not have it. The capability is an ability to undertake the management; the definition now says what that management is directed toward. The wording follows the reviewer's suggested refinement in substance. The genus field now names the immediate genus, bco:BusinessCapability: the class the definition's text names and bcom:BusinessCapability designates. cco:ont00000568 (Organization Capability) moved to foundational_ancestor (review R7 Finding E; docs/decisions/2026-10-25-r7-genus-decision.md). Nothing is minted."@en .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:changeNote "2026-11-07, tranche 2 (docs/decisions/2026-11-07-curation-tranche-2-approved.md): normalized from catalog candidate BCC-0ba10d44, with the alternative label its sources give and its broader concept, Financial Resource Management, as a component. The definition is unchanged."@en .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:definition "A business capability, inhering in an organization, that is realizable in planned acts by which that organization manages its cash positions, liquidity, funding and financial exposures toward meeting its financial obligations."@en .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:inScheme bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme .
bcoc:TreasuryManagement skos:prefLabel "Treasury Management"@en .

